## Linear Classifiers

Binary linear classifiers assign labels based on the sign of an affine discriminant function:

$$
g(\mathbf{x})=\mathbf{w}^\top\mathbf{x}+w_0.
$$

::: {.callout-note appearance="minimal"}
Definition. A binary linear classifier assigns class labels via:
$$
\widehat{y}=\operatorname{sign}(\mathbf{w}^\top\mathbf{x}+w_0),
\qquad \widehat{y}\in\{-1,+1\}.
$$ {#eq-linear-classifier}
:::

